3. If no such digit exists, return `false` (no bigger permutation possible)
4. Find the smallest digit to the right of index `i` that is larger than `digits[i]` (let's call its index `j`)
5. Swap `digits[i]` and `digits[j]`
6. Reverse the suffix starting at `i+1`
7. Convert back to a number and return it

